<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-NAB says Q1 net profit A$582 mln.</title>
<headline>RTRS-NAB says Q1 net profit A$582 mln.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>First quarter to Dec 31</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit			921 vs 781</p>
<p>    Net					 582 vs 513</p>
<p>NOTE: Full name is National Australia Bank Ltd.  </p>
<p>    Other income			    813 vs 682</p>
<p>    Interest income (billion)	  3.16 vs 2.97</p>
<p>    Interest expense (billion)	 1.85 vs 1.72</p>
<p>    Net interest income (billion)    1.32 vs 1.25</p>
<p>    Total income (billion)	     2.09 vs 1.88</p>
<p>    Doubtful debts charge		  39 vs 58</p>
<p>    Total assets (billion)	   184.02 vs 164.86</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			    39.4 vs 35.9</p>
<p>    Tax					8</p>
<p>    Depreciation			     19 vs 16</p>
<p>NOTE: Operating revenue by geographic segment</p>
<p>    Australia (billion)		  2.13 vs 2.00</p>
<p>    U.K. and Europe			 904 vs 867</p>
<p>    New Zealand			     534 vs 466</p>
<p>    U.S.					298 vs 239</p>
<p>    Asia					108 vs 87</p>
<p>NOTE: Operating profit after tax and goodwill by geographic segment.</p>
<p>    Australia				 376 vs 371</p>
<p>    U.K. and Europe			  94 vs 79</p>
<p>    New Zealand				66 vs 22</p>
<p>    U.S.					 40 vs 37</p>
<p>    Asia					  6 vs 4</p>
<p>--Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
